    {
      "id": "claim_21efd09424454fa589696828f4306343",
      "statement": "`findSessionFile()` locates a session log by scanning the `$DSH_HOME/sessions` workspace tree for `<workspace>/<sessionId>/session.jsonl.zstd`, returning the first existing file and `null` when none exists (which the `lifecycle` method turns into a thrown `找不到会话日志` error); the session id is validated against `^session-[A-Za-z0-9-]+$` before any filesystem access, preventing path traversal.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/index.ts#L306-L310",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6de266eb97fcc76326b6714767dc18a502aa484b084ad6011efedba990ea90c9:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/index.ts#L97-L117",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:40ef4f10418b660571ec6f1316a3087e411bfa2edb34102df340af82778eaa3a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_85b32a6e63b8456ea38cead51466a49d",
      "statement": "`decompressZstdFrames()` scans the byte buffer for the zstd frame magic bytes `28 B5 2F FD` and decompresses each frame independently with `zstdDecompressSync`, skipping a corrupt frame per-frame (never failing the whole trace) and returning an empty string when no magic bytes are found, so a truncated or non-zstd log degrades to zero events rather than throwing.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/index.ts#L76-L95",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9a41d1e808b95f19518d2292c7e25a9b4712c148c694131380d278921d3880af:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_a915977fa29a40ea89c872ea37e9a2f9",
      "statement": "The lifecycle parser splits the decoded JSONL text into lines, parses each as JSON inside a try/catch, and switches on `rec.type` to emit a flat `LifecycleEvent` with a `kind` the client understands while also updating scalar aggregates: `session/title` sets title, `turn/start` sets `turns`, `step/start` increments `steps`, `tool/call` increments `toolCalls`, `approval/asked` increments `approvals`, `todo/write` increments `todoWrites`; an unhandled record type yields no event and no counter change.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/index.ts#L325-L405",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b8bdad1bf655b908600ac9aeb206eeddcfaf3f960e817daf19367d8667a7b59a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_56106def36f84ee6a5f366c5b8a01712",
      "statement": "Turn and step counting differ deliberately because step numbering resets each turn: `turns` uses `Math.max(turns, turn)` over turn numbers while `steps` increments once per `step/start` event, which is the only reliable total step count.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/index.ts#L344-L355",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d5e6c63863f55298cd991b40a45bfa56a320290a401a13a623d107eb484d8595:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_260558b9850f44c99de195aacaca1e53",
      "statement": "The trace's long text and argument fields are bounded before crossing the boundary: `user`/`assistant` and `tool-result` text are truncated to 400 chars, and `tool-call` toolArgs plus `approval-asked` reason are truncated to 200 chars via `truncate()`, so a single huge tool result or message cannot bloat the flat event payload.",
      "evidence": [
        {
