    {
      "id": "claim_4ebdd770bfa54910b12990913eb232c2",
      "statement": "`compact()` strips own properties whose value is `undefined` and is required for the lifecycle result to pass the Typert boundary JSON-safety check: each event literal is compacted as it is pushed and the final snapshot is compacted again, because the zod-optional `turn`/`step`/`text`/`toolName`/`toolArgs`/`isError`/`outcome`/`reason`/`todos` fields are only sometimes present and an `undefined`-valued own property would be rejected as not JSON-safe.",
